<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴκτερ-ος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>jaundice</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				4.62
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Morb.</u>
				2.38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Int.</u>
				35
			</span></i>(pl.), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a bird of a yellowish-green colour</i>, by looking at which a
			jaundiced person was cured—the bird died! <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				30.94
			</span></i> (who identifies it with <i>galgulus</i>, the <i>golden
				oriole</i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
